 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the composition of\nthe Rochester-Genesee regional transportation authority",
    "basePrintNo": "S5389",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5389-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1299-dd, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5389\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the public authorities law, in\nrelation to the composition of the Rochester-Genesee regional transpor-\ntation authority\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide a representative of the transit dependent and/or disabled\ncommunity a non-voting position on the RGRTA Board of Commissioners.\nSuch a person would be appointed by the Governor.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends subdivision 1 of section 1299-dd of the public authorities law.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder current law, the RGRTA Board of Commissioners consists of twelve\nvoting members and one non-voting member representing the Authority's\nlargest labor organization. All members are recommended to, and\nappointed by, the governor with the advice and consent of the State\nSenate. With exception to the non-voting labor Member, the existing\nappointment process allows the governor to appoint board members from\nany group or constituency. The addition of a member of the region's\ntransit dependent/disabled community will facilitate input from those\ncommunities and result in better public service. The transit dependent\nand/or disabled community represents a significant percentage of the\nRGRTA ridership base. The appointment of this member will ensure that\ntheir interests are properly represented and taken into consideration by\nthe board. This member would also provide real time input from those\nconstituencies and help the RGRTA better serve and connect with riders.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2015-2016: A.466 - Passed Assembly\n2017-2018: A.201 - Passed Assembly\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
